Yes.

286
00:13:44,179 --> 00:13:47,512
They're over at the counter seats.

287
00:13:47,535 --> 00:13:49,185
Thank you!

288
00:13:49,208 --> 00:13:52,175
I'd like to use my laptop.

289
00:13:52,198 --> 00:13:55,398
I'll show you to the counter seats.

290
00:13:55,421 --> 00:13:57,698
This way, please.

291
00:13:57,722 --> 00:13:59,363
Thank you!

292
00:13:59,387 --> 00:14:02,220
Do you have Wi-Fi here?

293
00:14:02,243 --> 00:14:03,810
Yes.

294
00:14:03,833 --> 00:14:06,709
We offer free Wi-Fi.

295
00:14:06,732 --> 00:14:10,214
What's the password?

296
00:14:10,237 --> 00:14:13,735
It's written on the back of the menu.

297
00:14:13,759 --> 00:14:15,835
Please take a look here.

298
00:14:15,859 --> 00:14:17,893
Got it.

299
00:14:17,916 --> 00:14:19,984
That's a big help, thanks!

300
00:14:20,007 --> 00:14:24,274
May I ask a small favor?

301
00:14:24,297 --> 00:14:29,497
During busy times, we kindly ask for a maximum stay of two hours.

302
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,087
Yes.

303
00:14:31,110 --> 00:14:32,944
Got it.

304
00:14:32,967 --> 00:14:35,300
Got it.

305
00:14:35,323 --> 00:14:38,057
Thank you for your cooperation.

306
00:14:38,080 --> 00:14:41,494
Have you decided on your drink order?

307
00:14:41,517 --> 00:14:43,326
Yes.

308
00:14:43,349 --> 00:14:46,549
I'll have a hot coffee, please.

309
00:14:46,572 --> 00:14:49,548
What size would you like?

310
00:14:49,572 --> 00:14:52,459
I'll take a medium, please.

311
00:14:52,483 --> 00:14:54,561
Got it.

312
00:14:54,584 --> 00:14:57,817
Would you like sugar and milk?

313
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:01,040
One sugar, please.

314
00:15:01,063 --> 00:15:02,930
Got it.

315
00:15:02,953 --> 00:15:05,786
Please wait just a moment.

316
00:15:05,809 --> 00:15:07,309
Scene 8: Customer Service and a Comfortable Environment

317
00:15:07,309 --> 00:15:09,148
Welcome!

318
00:15:09,172 --> 00:15:12,816
Are you feeling cold, ma'am/sir?

319
00:15:12,839 --> 00:15:15,373
Oh, I'm sorry.

320
00:15:15,395 --> 00:15:18,162
It's a little chilly.

321
00:15:18,185 --> 00:15:20,818
I apologize for that.

322
00:15:20,841 --> 00:15:25,575
This spot gets direct airflow from the AC, doesn't it?

323
00:15:25,598 --> 00:15:27,164
Yes.

324
00:15:27,187 --> 00:15:30,221
The breeze is a bit strong.

325
00:15:30,244 --> 00:15:33,492
Shall I turn up the temperature a bit?

326
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:35,115
Yes, please.

327
00:15:35,138 --> 00:15:39,472
Also, do you have blankets?

328
00:15:39,495 --> 00:15:41,728
Yes, we do.

329
00:15:41,751 --> 00:15:44,686
I'll bring one right away.

330
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:46,315
Thank you!

331
00:15:46,338 --> 00:15:48,305
That's a big help, thanks!

332
00:15:48,328 --> 00:15:50,561
Thank you for waiting!

333
00:15:50,584 --> 00:15:54,051
Here's a blanket for you.

334
00:15:54,074 --> 00:15:55,679
Thank you!

335
00:15:55,703 --> 00:15:58,379
It's so warm!

336
00:15:58,402 --> 00:16:00,435
Great!

337
00:16:00,458 --> 00:16:05,192
Would you like to move to a different seat if that's alright?

338
00:16:05,215 --> 00:16:08,671
Yes, I'd like to move.

339
00:16:08,694 --> 00:16:12,301
Is the seating area in the back available?

340
00:16:12,325 --> 00:16:13,795
Yes.

341
00:16:13,819 --> 00:16:17,513
The square table in the back is open.

342
00:16:17,536 --> 00:16:20,936
Is it quiet over there?

343
00:16:20,959 --> 00:16:25,126
I'd like to relax and read a book today.

344
00:16:25,149 --> 00:16:26,282
Yes.

345
00:16:26,305 --> 00:16:29,572
The seats in the back are very quiet.

346
00:16:29,595 --> 00:16:32,473
And the air conditioning doesn't blow directly on you.

347
00:16:32,496 --> 00:16:34,766
That sounds great.

348
00:16:34,790 --> 00:16:38,324
Then, I'll take that seat over there.

349
00:16:38,347 --> 00:16:41,480
May I carry your bag for you?

350
00:16:41,503 --> 00:16:44,503
No, I'll carry it myself.

351
00:16:44,526 --> 00:16:46,659
I'm fine, thank you.

352
00:16:46,682 --> 00:16:48,376
Got it.

353
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:51,600
Allow me to show you to your seat.

354
00:16:51,622 --> 00:16:53,189
Thank you!

355
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:58,379
Oh, and could I also have a refill of hot black tea, please?

356
00:16:58,402 --> 00:17:00,568
Got it.

357
00:17:00,591 --> 00:17:03,648
Would plain tea be alright?

358
00:17:03,672 --> 00:17:05,311
Yes.

359
00:17:05,334 --> 00:17:07,811
Plain tea would be perfect, thank you.

360
00:17:07,835 --> 00:17:10,602
I'll bring it right away.

361
00:17:10,625 --> 00:17:13,442
Please enjoy your time.

362
00:17:13,466 --> 00:17:15,926
Thank you!

363
00:17:15,949 --> 00:17:17,449
Scene 9: Practice Kanji and Particles

364
00:17:17,449 --> 00:17:22,249
Let's study a lot today!

365
00:17:22,272 --> 00:17:24,639
Yes, let's do our best!

366
00:17:24,662 --> 00:17:28,628
We have a Japanese test next week, right?

367
00:17:28,651 --> 00:17:32,531
Yes, it's the N5 test.

368
00:17:32,555 --> 00:17:35,688
How's your studying coming along?

369
00:17:35,711 --> 00:17:40,978
Hmm, kanji are a bit tough.

370
00:17:41,001 --> 00:17:44,201
Which kanji are you finding difficult?

371
00:17:44,224 --> 00:17:48,224
The kanji for 'week' and 'write'.

372
00:17:48,247 --> 00:17:51,783
Ah, those kanji with lots of strokes.

373
00:17:51,806 --> 00:17:56,474
Yes, they're hard to memorize.

374
00:17:56,498 --> 00:17:59,631
You'll remember them if you write them repeatedly.

375
00:17:59,654 --> 00:18:03,832
You're right. I'll practice every day.

376
00:18:03,856 --> 00:18:06,136
How about grammar?

377
00:18:06,159 --> 00:18:09,572
I sometimes get confused with particles.

378
00:18:09,596 --> 00:18:12,670
Like the differences between 'ni' and 'de'?

379
00:18:12,694 --> 00:18:16,361
Yes, I often hesitate.

380
00:18:16,385 --> 00:18:20,427
Alright, let's quiz each other starting now.

381
00:18:20,450 --> 00:18:23,383
That sounds good. Please go ahead.

382
00:18:23,406 --> 00:18:26,475
Here's the first question.

383
00:18:26,499 --> 00:18:30,670
I study ___ the café.

384
00:18:30,694 --> 00:18:33,927
What particle fits in the blank?

385
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:38,232
Since it's a place, is it 'de'?

386
00:18:38,256 --> 00:18:40,505
Correct!

387
00:18:40,528 --> 00:18:42,995
Well done!

388
00:18:43,018 --> 00:18:46,385
Great, I feel relieved.

389
00:18:46,408 --> 00:18:50,490
Now, let me ask you a question.

390
00:18:50,513 --> 00:18:52,680
Sure, go ahead.

391
00:18:52,703 --> 00:18:57,073
Tomorrow, I wake up ___ 8 o'clock.

392
00:18:57,096 --> 00:19:01,764
What particle fits in the blank?

393
00:19:01,788 --> 00:19:06,054
Since it's after a time, it's 'ni,' right?

394
00:19:06,077 --> 00:19:08,052
Perfect!

395
00:19:08,075 --> 00:19:10,142
Impressive!

396
00:19:10,165 --> 00:19:14,062
Phew, I'm a little tired.

397
00:19:14,085 --> 00:19:17,852
My head is feeling a bit tired too.

398
00:19:17,875 --> 00:19:21,242
We've been studying for about an hour.

399
00:19:21,265 --> 00:19:24,398
Shall we take a short break?

400
00:19:24,421 --> 00:19:28,310
Yes, I could go for something sweet.

401
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:32,066
There’s cake in that case over there.

402
00:19:32,089 --> 00:19:35,823
That strawberry cake looks delicious!

403
00:19:35,846 --> 00:19:38,612
We also have chocolate cake.

404
00:19:38,635 --> 00:19:41,845
I’ll go with the strawberry cake.

405
00:19:41,869 --> 00:19:45,766
Then I’ll have the chocolate cake.

406
00:19:45,789 --> 00:19:48,723
Should we call the server over?

407
00:19:48,747 --> 00:19:51,429
Yes, let’s do that.

408
00:19:51,452 --> 00:19:52,952
Scene 10: Preparing for the Lunch Rush and Assigning Roles

409
00:19:52,952 --> 00:19:58,185
It’s almost 11:45.

410
00:19:58,208 --> 00:20:01,296
Lunchtime is coming up.

411
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:04,322
Yes, senior.

412
00:20:04,345 --> 00:20:07,678
The shop’s going to get busy soon.

413
00:20:07,701 --> 00:20:11,068
Let’s confirm our roles.

414
00:20:11,091 --> 00:20:15,091
You’re on the register today.

415
00:20:15,114 --> 00:20:17,247
Got it.

416
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:20,948
I’ll take orders at the register.

417
00:20:20,971 --> 00:20:25,619
I’ll handle the kitchen and drinks.

418
00:20:25,642 --> 00:20:29,076
I’ll make sandwiches and coffee.

419
00:20:29,099 --> 00:20:30,865
Yes.

420
00:20:30,888 --> 00:20:33,890
Are you all set?

421
00:20:33,914 --> 00:20:37,281
Do we have spoons and forks?

422
00:20:37,304 --> 00:20:41,312
Please check near the register.

423
00:20:41,336 --> 00:20:45,336
Oh, we’re low on spoons.

424
00:20:45,359 --> 00:20:48,492
I’ll restock them right away.

425
00:20:48,515 --> 00:20:50,392
Thanks.

426
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:54,883
Also, check the takeout bags and cups.

427
00:20:54,906 --> 00:20:56,514
Yes.

428
00:20:56,537 --> 00:21:00,004
We have plenty of bags and cups.

429
00:21:00,027 --> 00:21:03,270
Great!

430
00:21:03,294 --> 00:21:06,827
Don’t forget the straws.

431
00:21:06,850 --> 00:21:08,223
Got it.

432
00:21:08,247 --> 00:21:10,899
I’ve already prepared the straws.

433
00:21:10,922 --> 00:21:15,255
Next, let’s practice our greetings.

434
00:21:15,278 --> 00:21:18,812
Can you greet customers in a loud, clear voice?

435
00:21:18,835 --> 00:21:21,635
Yes, I can!

436
00:21:21,658 --> 00:21:23,671
Welcome!

437
00:21:23,694 --> 00:21:26,627
You have a great voice!

438
00:21:26,650 --> 00:21:29,983
And your smile is wonderful.

439
00:21:30,006 --> 00:21:31,904
Thank you!

440
00:21:31,928 --> 00:21:34,967
I’ll do my best today!

441
00:21:34,991 --> 00:21:39,057
Yes, let’s work hard together!

442
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:42,280
Customers are here!

443
00:21:42,303 --> 00:21:45,870
Welcome!

444
00:21:45,893 --> 00:21:47,393
Scene 11: Taking Orders and Checking for Allergies

445
00:21:47,393 --> 00:21:49,393
Welcome!

446
00:21:49,416 --> 00:21:52,383
Will you be dining in?

447
00:21:52,406 --> 00:21:56,006
Yes, we’ll eat here.

448
00:21:56,028 --> 00:21:57,662
Thank you!

449
00:21:57,685 --> 00:22:00,851
Are you ready to order?

450
00:22:00,874 --> 00:22:04,916
I’d like the daily sandwich set, please.

451
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:08,189
The daily sandwich set, got it.

452
00:22:08,212 --> 00:22:12,748
Today’s sandwich is chicken and vegetables.

453
00:22:12,771 --> 00:22:14,938
That looks delicious!

454
00:22:14,962 --> 00:22:17,260
I’ll take that.

455
00:22:17,283 --> 00:22:22,083
Do you have any food allergies, ma’am/sir?

456
00:22:22,106 --> 00:22:27,040
Yes, I’m allergic to eggs.

457
00:22:27,063 --> 00:22:29,496
Got it.

458
00:22:29,519 --> 00:22:34,286
The sandwich contains mayonnaise.

459
00:22:34,309 --> 00:22:38,309
Mayonnaise is made with eggs.

460
00:22:38,332 --> 00:22:40,415
I see.

461
00:22:40,438 --> 00:22:44,012
Can we remove the mayonnaise?

462
00:22:44,035 --> 00:22:48,475
Sure, I'll make it without mayonnaise.

463
00:22:48,498 --> 00:22:50,098
Thank you!

464
00:22:50,121 --> 00:22:52,140
That's a big help, thanks!

465
00:22:52,164 --> 00:22:55,964
What would you like to drink with your meal?

466
00:22:55,987 --> 00:22:58,387
What do you have?

467
00:22:58,410 --> 00:23:03,610
We have coffee, tea, and orange juice.

468
00:23:03,633 --> 00:23:06,718
I'll have a hot tea, please.

469
00:23:06,741 --> 00:23:09,708
Hot tea, coming right up.

470
00:23:09,731 --> 00:23:12,740
Your total comes to 1,000 yen.

471
00:23:12,764 --> 00:23:15,297
I'll pay in cash.

472
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:18,654
That's exactly 1,000 yen. Thank you.

473
00:23:18,676 --> 00:23:22,010
Please take this number card.

474
00:23:22,033 --> 00:23:24,099
Got it.

475
00:23:24,122 --> 00:23:28,165
We'll bring your order to your table when it's ready.

476
00:23:28,189 --> 00:23:30,989
Please wait at any available seat.

477
00:23:31,012 --> 00:23:33,645
Thank you!

478
00:23:33,668 --> 00:23:35,168
Scene 12: Payment Methods at Checkout

479
00:23:35,168 --> 00:23:36,935
Welcome!

480
00:23:36,958 --> 00:23:39,026
You're ready to check out?

481
00:23:39,050 --> 00:23:41,823
Yes, please.

482
00:23:41,846 --> 00:23:44,700
You've ordered the daily lunch set, correct?

483
00:23:44,723 --> 00:23:48,323
Your total is 980 yen.

484
00:23:48,346 --> 00:23:49,961
Got it.

485
00:23:49,985 --> 00:23:52,218
I'll pay in cash.

486
00:23:52,241 --> 00:23:54,419
Oh, I'm sorry.

487
00:23:54,443 --> 00:23:56,693
I don't have enough change.

488
00:23:56,716 --> 00:23:59,083
I don’t have a 1,000-yen bill either.

489
00:23:59,106 --> 00:24:01,472
You’ll be fine.

490
00:24:01,495 --> 00:24:05,162
You can also pay with e-money or a card.

491
00:24:05,185 --> 00:24:07,072
Great!

492
00:24:07,095 --> 00:24:09,174
I'll pay with my phone.

493
00:24:09,198 --> 00:24:11,772
Please scan this barcode.

494
00:24:11,795 --> 00:24:15,494
Okay, let me scan it.

495
00:24:15,517 --> 00:24:18,852
Hmm, the screen isn’t changing.

496
00:24:18,875 --> 00:24:21,409
Really? That’s odd.

497
00:24:21,432 --> 00:24:24,699
Your phone signal is weak.

498
00:24:24,723 --> 00:24:27,092
The app isn’t responding.

499
00:24:27,115 --> 00:24:30,449
We have free Wi-Fi in the store.

500
00:24:30,472 --> 00:24:33,705
Here’s the password to use.

501
00:24:33,728 --> 00:24:35,304
Thank you!

502
00:24:35,327 --> 00:24:39,728
But that might take a while.

503
00:24:39,751 --> 00:24:42,485
There are other customers waiting behind you.

504
00:24:42,508 --> 00:24:45,324
Do you have a credit card?

505
00:24:45,348 --> 00:24:48,348
Yes, I have a card.

506
00:24:48,371 --> 00:24:51,504
You can pay by card as well.

507
00:24:51,527 --> 00:24:54,370
Then I’ll pay by card, please.

508
00:24:54,394 --> 00:24:57,794
Please tap your card here.

509
00:24:57,817 --> 00:24:59,583
I’ve tapped it.

510
00:24:59,606 --> 00:25:02,142
Payment complete.

511
00:25:02,166 --> 00:25:04,966
Please take your receipt.

512
00:25:04,989 --> 00:25:06,766
You saved me—thank you!

513
00:25:06,789 --> 00:25:08,589
Thank you!

514
00:25:08,612 --> 00:25:12,146
No problem, come again soon!

515
00:25:12,169 --> 00:25:13,669
Scene 13: Planning Your Trip

516
00:25:13,669 --> 00:25:18,035
This sandwich is absolutely delicious!

517
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:23,525
Yes, my egg sandwich is pretty amazing too.

518
00:25:23,548 --> 00:25:28,081
Today, let’s talk about next month’s trip.

519
00:25:28,104 --> 00:25:32,562
Sure, let’s plan our Kyoto trip.

520
00:25:32,585 --> 00:25:34,681
When should we go?

521
00:25:34,705 --> 00:25:37,913
How about the 10th of next month?

522
00:25:37,937 --> 00:25:41,870
Let’s go from Friday to Sunday.

523
00:25:41,893 --> 00:25:43,726
Perfect.

524
00:25:43,749 --> 00:25:46,482
That’s a 3-day, 2-night trip.

525
00:25:46,505 --> 00:25:49,305
Let’s take the Shinkansen.

526
00:25:49,328 --> 00:25:53,695
When should we buy the Shinkansen tickets?

527
00:25:53,718 --> 00:25:57,318
I’ll book them online next week.

528
00:25:57,341 --> 00:25:59,308
Got it.

529
00:25:59,331 --> 00:26:02,897
An early morning Shinkansen would be great.

530
00:26:02,920 --> 00:26:07,720
Yeah, let’s take the 8 AM Shinkansen.

531
00:26:07,743 --> 00:26:11,577
Once we arrive in Kyoto, where do you want to go?

532
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:15,215
I’d love to visit some famous temples.

533
00:26:15,238 --> 00:26:18,053
Let’s go to Kiyomizu-dera!

534
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:21,966
Kiyomizu-dera is so beautiful.

535
00:26:21,989 --> 00:26:26,645
I’d also like to see some old shrines.

536
00:26:26,669 --> 00:26:30,149
Then let’s visit Fushimi Inari Taisha too!

537
00:26:30,172 --> 00:26:31,774
Perfect.

538
00:26:31,798 --> 00:26:35,610
I’d love to check out some cozy cafés in Kyoto.

539
00:26:35,633 --> 00:26:39,000
Let’s try matcha ice cream!

540
00:26:39,023 --> 00:26:41,081
I’m so excited!

541
00:26:41,104 --> 00:26:44,271
Where should we stay?

542
00:26:44,294 --> 00:26:47,900
A hotel near Kyoto Station would be convenient.

543
00:26:47,924 --> 00:26:50,621
What’s our budget?

544
00:26:50,644 --> 00:26:53,977
I think around 50,000 yen per person.

545
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,972
Got it.

546
00:26:55,996 --> 00:27:00,207
The Shinkansen and hotel will cost about 30,000 yen.

547
00:27:00,230 --> 00:27:03,463
That leaves 20,000 yen for food and shopping.

548
00:27:03,486 --> 00:27:05,737
That sounds perfect.

549
00:27:05,761 --> 00:27:10,094
I’ll book the hotel tonight.

550
00:27:10,117 --> 00:27:11,684
Thanks!

551
00:27:11,707 --> 00:27:13,907
Nice to work with you!

552
00:27:13,930 --> 00:27:15,465
Yes.

553
00:27:15,488 --> 00:27:18,340
Let’s make this a fun trip!

554
00:27:18,363 --> 00:27:19,863
Scene 14: The Lunchtime Rush and Closing the Register

555
00:27:19,863 --> 00:27:22,333
Great job today!

556
00:27:22,357 --> 00:27:26,047
The lunchtime rush is finally over.

557
00:27:26,070 --> 00:27:28,313
Great job today!

558
00:27:28,336 --> 00:27:32,170
It was so busy today!

559
00:27:32,193 --> 00:27:33,999
Yes.

560
00:27:34,022 --> 00:27:38,115
We had so many customers.

561
00:27:38,139 --> 00:27:41,539
We sold a ton of sandwiches.

562
00:27:41,562 --> 00:27:44,702
And lots of juice too!

563
00:27:44,725 --> 00:27:48,691
Alright, let’s do the mid-shift register count.

564
00:27:48,714 --> 00:27:51,581
Please count the money.

565
00:27:51,604 --> 00:27:53,776
Got it.

566
00:27:53,799 --> 00:27:56,999
I’ll count the cash in the register.

567
00:27:57,022 --> 00:28:00,422
How many 1,000-yen bills are there?

568
00:28:00,445 --> 00:28:04,312
There are twenty 1,000-yen bills.

569
00:28:04,335 --> 00:28:07,501
What about 500-yen coins?

570
00:28:07,524 --> 00:28:11,262
There are ten 500-yen coins.

571
00:28:11,285 --> 00:28:15,324
Let’s confirm the total amount.

572
00:28:15,348 --> 00:28:18,630
Does it match the computer’s total?

573
00:28:18,653 --> 00:28:20,520
Yes.

574
00:28:20,543 --> 00:28:23,310
Yes, the amounts match.

575
00:28:23,333 --> 00:28:26,300
Great!

576
00:28:26,323 --> 00:28:29,256
The register count is done.

577
00:28:29,279 --> 00:28:31,412
That’s a relief!

578
00:28:31,435 --> 00:28:34,002
Are we taking a break now?

579
00:28:34,025 --> 00:28:35,663
Yes.

580
00:28:35,687 --> 00:28:39,220
Let’s take turns and rest for 15 minutes.

581
00:28:39,243 --> 00:28:43,416
You go first.

582
00:28:43,439 --> 00:28:45,092
Thank you!

583
00:28:45,116 --> 00:28:47,974
Can I have something to drink?

584
00:28:47,997 --> 00:28:49,637
Yeah, we did.

585
00:28:49,661 --> 00:28:53,027
Feel free to make yourself a drink.

586
00:28:53,050 --> 00:28:56,184
I’ll have some iced tea.

587
00:28:56,207 --> 00:29:00,007
I’ll add a little sugar.

588
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:03,363
Take it easy in the break room.

589
00:29:03,386 --> 00:29:07,243
Please come back in fifteen minutes.

590
00:29:07,267 --> 00:29:08,883
Yes.

591
00:29:08,906 --> 00:29:11,740
I'll take over when you return.

592
00:29:11,763 --> 00:29:13,996
Nice to work with you!

593
00:29:14,019 --> 00:29:16,619
Let's do our best this afternoon too!

594
00:29:16,642 --> 00:29:18,142
Scene 15: How to Order at a Café

595
00:29:18,142 --> 00:29:20,011
Welcome!

596
00:29:20,035 --> 00:29:22,803
Please take any seat you like.

597
00:29:22,826 --> 00:29:24,710
Thank you!

598
00:29:24,734 --> 00:29:27,067
I'll sit here.

599
00:29:27,091 --> 00:29:31,105
Please let us know when you're ready to order.

600
00:29:31,128 --> 00:29:32,766
Excuse me.

601
00:29:32,789 --> 00:29:35,237
I'd like to place my order.

602
00:29:35,261 --> 00:29:36,994
Yes.

603
00:29:37,017 --> 00:29:39,631
May I take your order?

604
00:29:39,655 --> 00:29:43,188
I'm craving something sweet.

605
00:29:43,211 --> 00:29:46,145
Do you have any recommended cakes?

606
00:29:46,168 --> 00:29:49,846
Our autumn-limited cake is highly recommended.

607
00:29:49,869 --> 00:29:52,515
The chestnut cake is very popular.

608
00:29:52,539 --> 00:29:54,984
Chestnut cake, you say?

609
00:29:55,007 --> 00:29:57,174
That looks delicious!

610
00:29:57,197 --> 00:30:00,472
The matcha parfait is also a favorite.

611
00:30:00,495 --> 00:30:03,429
Both sound wonderful.

612
00:30:03,452 --> 00:30:05,261
I can't decide!

613
00:30:05,284 --> 00:30:09,183
The chestnut cake isn't too sweet.

614
00:30:09,206 --> 00:30:11,539
It pairs well with coffee.

615
00:30:11,562 --> 00:30:13,529
I see.

616
00:30:13,552 --> 00:30:16,752
Then I'll go with the chestnut cake.

617
00:30:16,775 --> 00:30:18,392
Thank you!

618
00:30:18,416 --> 00:30:21,049
Would you like something to drink?

619
00:30:21,072 --> 00:30:23,907
I'll have a hot coffee, please.

620
00:30:23,930 --> 00:30:27,788
The cake and coffee set is a great deal.

621
00:30:27,812 --> 00:30:30,661
You save 50 yen with the set.

622
00:30:30,685 --> 00:30:33,251
That sounds great.

623
00:30:33,274 --> 00:30:35,453
I'll take the set, please.

624
00:30:35,477 --> 00:30:37,610
Got it.

625
00:30:37,633 --> 00:30:41,766
So that's the chestnut cake and a hot coffee.

626
00:30:41,789 --> 00:30:43,437
Yes.

627
00:30:43,461 --> 00:30:45,461
Nice to work with you!

628
00:30:45,484 --> 00:30:47,817
Please wait just a moment.

629
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:51,007
We'll bring it to your table.

630
00:30:51,030 --> 00:30:52,630
Got it.

631
00:30:52,653 --> 00:30:55,224
I'm looking forward to it!

632
00:30:55,247 --> 00:30:56,747
Scene 16: How to Make New Lattes

633
00:30:56,747 --> 00:31:00,222
It's a bit quiet now, isn't it?

634
00:31:00,245 --> 00:31:04,212
Let's practice making the new menu items.

635
00:31:04,235 --> 00:31:06,368
Yes, please.

636
00:31:06,391 --> 00:31:11,125
We're introducing new lattes starting next month.

637
00:31:11,148 --> 00:31:14,714
Matcha latte and caramel latte.

638
00:31:14,737 --> 00:31:17,771
They both sound delicious!

639
00:31:17,794 --> 00:31:20,927
Is the recipe difficult?

640
00:31:20,950 --> 00:31:23,750
Not at all!

641
00:31:23,773 --> 00:31:27,773
Let's start with the caramel latte.

642
00:31:27,796 --> 00:31:31,929
Okay, I'll prepare the cup.

643
00:31:31,952 --> 00:31:36,204
Add 15 grams of caramel syrup.

644
00:31:36,227 --> 00:31:39,044
Please measure it carefully with a spoon.

645
00:31:39,068 --> 00:31:41,868
15 grams, right?

646
00:31:41,891 --> 00:31:44,425
The syrup is in.

647
00:31:44,448 --> 00:31:48,814
Next, add the espresso.

648
00:31:48,837 --> 00:31:51,471
Just press the button once.

649
00:31:51,494 --> 00:31:54,761
Adding the espresso now.

650
00:31:54,784 --> 00:31:57,718
It smells amazing!

651
00:31:57,741 --> 00:32:01,478
After that, warm the milk.

652
00:32:01,501 --> 00:32:05,747
Froth it finely with steam.

653
00:32:05,771 --> 00:32:08,811
What temperature should the milk be?

654
00:32:08,834 --> 00:32:12,319
65 degrees is ideal.

655
00:32:12,343 --> 00:32:15,810
If it's too hot, it won't taste as good.

656
00:32:15,833 --> 00:32:17,966
Got it.

657
00:32:17,989 --> 00:32:21,088
Heated to 65 degrees.

658
00:32:21,111 --> 00:32:24,547
Gently pour in the milk.

659
00:32:24,571 --> 00:32:28,804
Drizzle caramel sauce on top.

660
00:32:28,827 --> 00:32:30,594
It's ready!

661
00:32:30,617 --> 00:32:32,954
It turned out beautifully.

662
00:32:32,977 --> 00:32:35,344
How does it taste?

663
00:32:35,367 --> 00:32:38,767
It's so sweet and delicious.

664
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:42,057
Next, let's make a matcha latte.

665
00:32:42,080 --> 00:32:46,713
Make sure to dissolve the matcha powder well in hot water.

666
00:32:46,736 --> 00:32:48,269
Yes.

667
00:32:48,292 --> 00:32:50,959
Whisk it thoroughly.

668
00:32:50,982 --> 00:32:52,482
Scene 17: How to Find Lost Items

669
00:32:52,482 --> 00:32:54,415
Welcome!

670
00:32:54,438 --> 00:32:56,405
Hello.

671
00:32:56,428 --> 00:32:58,280
Excuse me.

672
00:32:58,303 --> 00:33:01,313
I'm looking for something I lost.

673
00:33:01,337 --> 00:33:04,142
A lost item, you say?

674
00:33:04,165 --> 00:33:08,165
Did you come here today?

675
00:33:08,188 --> 00:33:09,963
Yes.

676
00:33:09,987 --> 00:33:14,120
I came around 12:30 today.

677
00:33:14,143 --> 00:33:16,149
Got it.

678
00:33:16,173 --> 00:33:19,506
Which seat did you sit in?

679
00:33:19,529 --> 00:33:23,605
The seat near the window in the back.

680
00:33:23,628 --> 00:33:27,228
I left it on the table.

681
00:33:27,251 --> 00:33:31,384
What did you lose?

682
00:33:31,407 --> 00:33:36,262
A black folding umbrella and a small bag.

683
00:33:36,286 --> 00:33:39,087
Could you describe them in more detail?

684
00:33:39,110 --> 00:33:42,577
What does the umbrella look like?

685
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:46,733
It's a small, black folding umbrella.

686
00:33:46,756 --> 00:33:50,495
There's a blue sticker on the handle.

687
00:33:50,518 --> 00:33:54,252
What kind of bag is it?

688
00:33:54,275 --> 00:33:57,935
It's a brown leather bag.

689
00:33:57,958 --> 00:34:00,451
It has two pockets.

690
00:34:00,474 --> 00:34:02,722
Got it.

691
00:34:02,746 --> 00:34:06,583
I'll check the storage in the back.

692
00:34:06,606 --> 00:34:09,039
Please wait just a moment.

693
00:34:09,062 --> 00:34:10,747
Yes.

694
00:34:10,770 --> 00:34:13,041
Nice to work with you!

695
00:34:13,065 --> 00:34:15,498
Thank you for waiting!

696
00:34:15,521 --> 00:34:17,795
Is this it?

697
00:34:17,818 --> 00:34:19,955
Oh, yes!

698
00:34:19,979 --> 00:34:22,983
That's my umbrella and bag!

699
00:34:23,006 --> 00:34:25,740
Thank you so much!

700
00:34:25,763 --> 00:34:28,129
Great!

701
00:34:28,152 --> 00:34:32,219
For confirmation, may I have your name?

702
00:34:32,242 --> 00:34:34,861
Tanaka.

703
00:34:34,885 --> 00:34:37,218
Kenta Tanaka.

704
00:34:37,241 --> 00:34:39,808
Mr. Tanaka, correct?

705
00:34:39,831 --> 00:34:43,398
Please write your name on this paper.

706
00:34:43,421 --> 00:34:45,354
Yes.

707
00:34:45,377 --> 00:34:47,235
I've written it.

708
00:34:47,259 --> 00:34:48,937
Thank you!

709
00:34:48,961 --> 00:34:51,894
Here are your lost items.

710
00:34:51,917 --> 00:34:54,093
You saved me—thank you!

711
00:34:54,117 --> 00:34:57,090
Thank you so much!

712
00:34:57,114 --> 00:35:01,651
You're welcome. We look forward to your next visit.

713
00:35:01,675 --> 00:35:03,175
Scene 18: Request for Leave Due to an Important Exam

714
00:35:03,175 --> 00:35:05,655
Good work today.

715
00:35:05,679 --> 00:35:09,279
Do you have a moment now?

716
00:35:09,302 --> 00:35:11,868
Good work today.

717
00:35:11,891 --> 00:35:14,925
Yes, it's fine.

718
00:35:14,947 --> 00:35:18,200
Actually, I need to talk to you about something.

719
00:35:18,224 --> 00:35:21,990
It's about next Saturday.

720
00:35:22,013 --> 00:35:25,147
Next Saturday, you say?

721
00:35:25,170 --> 00:35:27,446
What's the matter?

722
00:35:27,469 --> 00:35:31,802
There's a test next Saturday.

723
00:35:31,825 --> 00:35:35,281
It's an important exam for university.

724
00:35:35,305 --> 00:35:37,485
I see.

725
00:35:37,508 --> 00:35:40,041
Tests are tough, aren't they?

726
00:35:40,064 --> 00:35:41,998
Yes.

727
00:35:42,021 --> 00:35:46,319
That's why I want to take the day off work.

728
00:35:46,342 --> 00:35:48,217
Got it.

729
00:35:48,241 --> 00:35:51,974
I'm free this Saturday.

730
00:35:51,997 --> 00:35:54,164
Really?

731
00:35:54,187 --> 00:35:58,477
Could you cover my shift for me?

732
00:35:58,500 --> 00:36:01,700
Sure, no problem.

733
00:36:01,723 --> 00:36:04,132
I'll work on Saturday.

734
00:36:04,156 --> 00:36:07,043
Thank you so much!

735
00:36:07,067 --> 00:36:09,400
That's a huge help.

736
00:36:09,423 --> 00:36:13,482
No worries, happy to help.

737
00:36:13,505 --> 00:36:16,605
Good luck with your exam studies!

738
00:36:16,628 --> 00:36:19,638
Thanks, I'll do my best!

739
00:36:19,662 --> 00:36:24,596
In return, I'll work your Sunday shift.

740
00:36:24,619 --> 00:36:27,285
Sunday?

741
00:36:27,308 --> 00:36:31,075
That's my Sunday shift, right?

742
00:36:31,098 --> 00:36:32,751
Yes.

743
00:36:32,775 --> 00:36:37,741
I'll cover your shift on Sunday.

744
00:36:37,764 --> 00:36:39,531
Thank you!

745
00:36:39,554 --> 00:36:42,887
Then I'll take you up on that for Sunday.

746
00:36:42,910 --> 00:36:46,444
Got it!

747
00:36:46,467 --> 00:36:49,435
I'll let the manager know too.

748
00:36:49,458 --> 00:36:52,335
Thanks, I appreciate it.

749
00:36:52,358 --> 00:36:55,158
Thanks for always looking out for me.

750
00:36:55,181 --> 00:36:59,582
Next time, I'll buy you a nice juice!

751
00:36:59,605 --> 00:37:01,539
Hehe, thank you!

752
00:37:01,562 --> 00:37:04,832
Alright, let's wrap up our break.

753
00:37:04,855 --> 00:37:08,855
Yes, let's get back to work.

754
00:37:08,878 --> 00:37:10,378
Scene 19: The Basics of Customer Service

755
00:37:10,378 --> 00:37:12,231
Excuse me.

756
00:37:12,254 --> 00:37:14,295
Excuse me.

757
00:37:14,319 --> 00:37:17,253
Yes, how can I help you?

758
00:37:17,275 --> 00:37:22,076
Thank you for always choosing our store.

759
00:37:22,100 --> 00:37:25,634
We'll be closing soon at 8 PM.

760
00:37:25,657 --> 00:37:29,057
Oh, is it that time already?

761
00:37:29,080 --> 00:37:31,113
Got it.

762
00:37:31,136 --> 00:37:34,936
May I take your empty cup?

763
00:37:34,959 --> 00:37:37,492
Yes, please.

764
00:37:37,515 --> 00:37:39,963
This cup, right?

765
00:37:39,987 --> 00:37:41,787
Thank you!

766
00:37:41,810 --> 00:37:44,410
I'll take it for you.

767
00:37:44,433 --> 00:37:47,110
Please take your time getting ready.

768
00:37:47,134 --> 00:37:51,568
Okay, I'll pack up my things right away.

769
00:37:51,591 --> 00:37:54,558
You can pay at the register.

770
00:37:54,581 --> 00:37:58,514
Today, we accept both cash and credit cards.

771
00:37:58,537 --> 00:38:01,196
I'll pay with a credit card.

772
00:38:01,219 --> 00:38:04,553
I'll put my jacket on and head to the register.

773
00:38:04,576 --> 00:38:06,176
Got it.

774
00:38:06,199 --> 00:38:08,933
I'll be waiting for you at the register.

775
00:38:08,956 --> 00:38:10,723
Excuse me.

776
00:38:10,746 --> 00:38:12,963
May I have the bill, please?

777
00:38:12,986 --> 00:38:16,961
Sure, that's a hot coffee and a cake, right?

778
00:38:16,985 --> 00:38:19,918
Your total comes to 800 yen.

779
00:38:19,941 --> 00:38:21,874
I'll pay by card, please.

780
00:38:21,897 --> 00:38:24,331
I'll take your card.

781
00:38:24,354 --> 00:38:27,052
Would you like to pay in full?

782
00:38:27,076 --> 00:38:30,443
Yes, in full, please.

783
00:38:30,467 --> 00:38:33,345
Here's your receipt and card.

784
00:38:33,368 --> 00:38:35,535
Please check.

785
00:38:35,558 --> 00:38:37,326
Thank you!

786
00:38:37,349 --> 00:38:40,205
That coffee was absolutely delicious.

787
00:38:40,229 --> 00:38:41,766
Thank you!

788
00:38:41,790 --> 00:38:44,757
I'm so glad you liked it.

789
00:38:44,780 --> 00:38:48,980
It's really cold tonight, so please take care.

790
00:38:49,003 --> 00:38:50,848
Thank you!

791
00:38:50,871 --> 00:38:53,038
I'll be back.

792
00:38:53,061 --> 00:38:54,718
Thank you!

793
00:38:54,742 --> 00:38:58,775
We sincerely look forward to your next visit.

794
00:38:58,798 --> 00:39:01,365
Have a wonderful evening.

795
00:39:01,388 --> 00:39:04,032
Have a wonderful evening.

796
00:39:04,055 --> 00:39:05,555
Scene 20: Closing Time – Counting Today’s Sales

797
00:39:05,555 --> 00:39:08,394
Great job today, everyone.

798
00:39:08,417 --> 00:39:11,550
Did you lock the front door?

799
00:39:11,573 --> 00:39:14,252
Yes, I did.

800
00:39:14,276 --> 00:39:18,409
I brought the outdoor sign inside too.

801
00:39:18,432 --> 00:39:20,286
Thanks!

802
00:39:20,310 --> 00:39:24,545
Alright, let’s count the cash in the register.

803
00:39:24,568 --> 00:39:28,020
Sure, I’ll count it.

804
00:39:28,044 --> 00:39:31,977
There are twenty 1,000-yen bills.

805
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:35,659
How many 5,000-yen bills are there?

806
00:39:35,683 --> 00:39:39,250
There are four 5,000-yen bills.

807
00:39:39,273 --> 00:39:43,075
And six 10,000-yen bills, right?

808
00:39:43,098 --> 00:39:45,532
I counted the coins too.

809
00:39:45,555 --> 00:39:48,488
What’s today’s total sales?

810
00:39:48,511 --> 00:39:51,678
It’s 100,000 yen.

811
00:39:51,701 --> 00:39:54,120
That’s fantastic!

812
00:39:54,143 --> 00:39:57,279
It matches the register total.

813
00:39:57,302 --> 00:39:59,240
Great!

814
00:39:59,264 --> 00:40:02,330
Should we take out the trash next?

815
00:40:02,353 --> 00:40:04,410
Yes, please.

816
00:40:04,434 --> 00:40:07,967
Please gather the kitchen trash bags.

817
00:40:07,990 --> 00:40:09,842
Got it.

818
00:40:09,865 --> 00:40:13,151
I’ll take them to the back trash area.

819
00:40:13,174 --> 00:40:16,642
I’ll write in the logbook.

820
00:40:16,666 --> 00:40:20,099
I’ll notify the morning staff.

821
00:40:20,122 --> 00:40:22,356
What are you writing?

822
00:40:22,380 --> 00:40:26,350
I’ll note that we’re running low on milk.

823
00:40:26,374 --> 00:40:32,007
I’ll ask them to buy new milk tomorrow morning.

824
00:40:32,030 --> 00:40:34,597
That’s important.

825
00:40:34,620 --> 00:40:37,293
Finished taking out the trash.

826
00:40:37,316 --> 00:40:40,329
Please turn off the lights and air conditioning.

827
00:40:40,353 --> 00:40:42,753
Okay, I turned them off.

828
00:40:42,776 --> 00:40:45,634
Did we forget anything?

829
00:40:45,657 --> 00:40:48,590
No, we’re all set.

830
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:50,981
Alright, let’s head home.

831
00:40:51,005 --> 00:40:54,343
Thank you all for another great day.

832
00:40:54,366 --> 00:40:56,700
Great job today!

833
00:40:56,723 --> 00:40:59,656
See you tomorrow.